## Working Rules

- Keep the app buildable. Verify meaningful code changes with
  `{{GOVERNANCE_CHECK_COMMAND}}`, `{{TYPECHECK_COMMAND}}`, and
  `{{BUILD_COMMAND}}`; add `{{GOVERNANCE_RUN_GATES_COMMAND}}` when an active
  Micro-Spec is driving the work.
- Only `status: active` Micro-Specs can drive implementation. Treat the
  governance docs as governance-only unless an active spec exists.
- Scaffold new specs with `governance:new-spec`; change a spec's lifecycle
  status only through `governance:advance` (it runs the gates fresh and
  records the evidence ledger). Never hand-edit `status:` lines or ledger
  files under `micro-specs/evidence/`.
- For risky, cross-cutting, security, data, billing, auth, migration, or
  production-adjacent work, create or activate a Micro-Spec first.
- Server state remains authoritative. Browser storage is cache only; changes
  affecting money, permissions, identity, or audit trails must stay
  server-side and provable by durable (non-browser-only) tests.
- Read the relevant local framework docs before changing routing, data
  mutation, auth, or configuration. Prefer in-repo docs over memory.
- Keep governance current-only. Add planning packs, generated route docs,
  screenshot/evidence folders, or design-source mirrors only when explicitly
  asked.
- Preserve existing user work. Check `git status` before destructive commands,
  commits, or broad rewrites.

## Governance Files

- `AGENTS.md` — repository working rules and routing.
- `Instructions_MicroSpecsCreation.md` — how to author Micro-Specs.
- `Instructions_tdd.md` — implementation workflow when a Micro-Spec is active.
- `micro-specs/README.md` — governance index, lifecycle, risk classes, gates.
- `micro-specs/GLOBAL_CONTEXT.md` — reusable, repo-specific constraints.
- `scripts/check-governance.mjs` — validates metadata, risk gates, blast radius.
- `scripts/run-governance-gates.mjs` — runs gates declared by active Micro-Specs.

## Validation Baseline

- Install: `{{INSTALL_COMMAND}}`
- Lint: `{{LINT_COMMAND}}`
- Typecheck: `{{TYPECHECK_COMMAND}}`
- Test: `{{TEST_COMMAND}}`
- Build: `{{BUILD_COMMAND}}`
- Governance check: `{{GOVERNANCE_CHECK_COMMAND}}`
- Active gates: `{{GOVERNANCE_RUN_GATES_COMMAND}}` (repeat `--spec <id>` to
  batch a deduplicated multi-spec proof; add `--record` for per-spec ledgers)
- New spec: `governance:new-spec --id MS-<area>-<slug> --risk <class> --title "<text>"`
- Lifecycle: `governance:advance <spec-id> --to <status>`

If a command is missing, inspect the repository and update this guide with the
correct command instead of inventing one.
